## Program Constraints

- Findings are bounded operational diagnostics tied to authoritative revisions, not a parallel
  outcome or campaign system.
- Local resolution always refreshes project identity and state; copied commands never embed a
  path, token, disposition, or pre-authorized mutation.
- Historical automation discovers, groups, proposes, applies exact reviewed manifests, and
  verifies; it never supplies ambiguous semantic judgment.
- Reporter and hosted fields remain allowlisted, controlled, capped, and source-specific.
- Hosted pages consume commands only from a shared controlled action descriptor or an exact
  allowlisted built-in route. Pages never construct target-specific commands from display text.
- Copy controls appear only for currently supported local routes. Resolved history and ordinary
  navigation do not imply an actionable command.
- Work2 changes development only. Work3 freezes and qualifies. Work5 production promotion remains
  a separate explicit route.

## Verification Strategy

- Assert stable finding identity, deduplication, first/last observation, source revision,
  resolution, recurrence, migration, checkpoint/rebuild parity, and bounded cardinality.
- Compare local finding rows, report payloads, hosted rows, view models, and browser-visible text and
  clipboard values exactly while also proving forbidden fields are absent.
- Assert the shared copy component on every applicable hosted page and its absence for unsupported
  or historical-only rows.
- Exercise stale, wrong-workspace, missing, already-resolved, ambiguous, and protected-action cases.
- Verify every historical manifest against the complete scanned surface and rerun document,
  outcome, lineage, evidence, propagation, and release audits after mutation.

